It's true that in any dungeon *tree* visiting the lowest level counts
as visiting all the levels. But I'm not really sure now how the "levels
visited" is computed when you include the other trees. I believe the
mine and quest levels get numbers starting with 56 or so, i.e *below*
the Sanctum. At least, the alock.* files have these numbers.

While on the subject, there's a feature I'd like to see (yo devteam!) in
the next release. When you have tport control and do a level tport, you
are asked to type a number. It would be nice at this point to have a ?
option that lists the levels visited. This would involve no extra code,
as this is just equivalent to the ^O option of wizard mode, with a minor
mod to list only the levels visited.

Since your adventurer seems to remember every level she ever visits in
excruciating detail, it seems only natural she should be able to summon
up a map of the dungeon tree as well.

